# A traveller books a ferry and cancels it again, in Island Hop.
# Payments are off on a local backend (no PAYMENTS_ENABLED), so a booking is confirmed straight
# away and nothing is charged. Cancelling gives the seats back, so the trip is as it was.
# The traveller is a seeded account (prisma/seed.ts).

Test: A traveller books two seats and cancels the booking

  As traveller:
    go to "/ferries?from=Blowing Point, Anguilla&to=Marigot, Saint Martin&departureDate={tomorrow}&adults=2&passengers=2 Passengers"
    click "Select Trip"
    click "Continue to Passenger Details"
    click "Continue to Payment"
    click "Continue to pay"
    backend should receive POST /api/v1/bookings
    backend should reply 201 Created
    click "Manage booking"
    click "Cancel Booking"
    in "Cancel Booking" dialog, click "Confirm Cancellation"
    backend should receive PATCH /api/v1/bookings/:id/cancel
    backend should reply 200 OK
    should see "Booking cancelled successfully"
